From 8bf4551bc20d585cf64a023ec8a954c43ea19a1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:58:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 8864: fix QoS Null probes with active BA sessions

mac80211 sends client probes as QoS Null frames without A-MPDU handling.
If the peer already has an active transmit BA session for the probe's
TID, the 88W8864 transmit path incorrectly applies its Block Ack
assertion and drops the probe.

Exclude QoS Null frames from aggregation handling.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 hif/pcie/8864/tx.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
@@ -732,7 +732,8 @@ void pcie_8864_tx_xmit(struct ieee80211_
 
 	if (sta && sta->deflink.ht_cap.ht_supported &&
 	  !(xmitcontrol & EAGLE_TXD_XMITCTRL_USE_MC_RATE) &&
-	    ieee80211_is_data_qos(wh->frame_control)) {
+	    ieee80211_is_data_qos(wh->frame_control) &&
+	    !ieee80211_is_qos_nullfunc(wh->frame_control)) {
 		tid = qos & 0xf;
 		pcie_tx_count_packet(sta, tid);
 
